# T-029: the Cloudflare tunnel of podnet. The commit holds the bound check
# of capnp.rs (podnet 54637d9, PodUtils/podnet#555) and the reconnect of the
# leg quic+warp (podnet eb23c379, PodUtils/podnet#603).
# race.rs: the race of the legs (crates/podnet-core). yaml.rs: the reader of
# the configuration file that config.rs uses (crates/podnet-core).
# ingress.rs: the ingress rules of the configuration file
# (crates/podnet-serve); the services of podnet go behind ServiceDispatch.
# ws.rs: the edge side only (serve_websocket, forward_path, forward_url,
# DEFAULT_PATH); the rest stays in podnet. fuzzing.rs: the targets of the
# edge only. tools/: the oracle of the header encoding of cloudflared, and
# the check of the pin of cloudflared (the paths of the crate).
# origin.rs: the dial of a forward origin (crates/podnet-serve). metrics.rs:
# the counters of a tunnel (crates/podnet-core). udp.rs: the UDP probe of the
# edge and its choice (crates/podnet-core); the variables stay in podnet.
# Parts of files that the drift check does not follow, taken in the
# adaptation: crates/podnet-core/src/net.rs (local_name, split_host_port,
# connect_origin, parse_http_url, with their tests) in origin.rs;
# crates/podnet-core/src/report.rs (clean) in text.rs;
# crates/podnet-core/src/util/mod.rs (validate_quick_hostname and its test
# quick_hosts) in quicktunnel.rs, (authority_of, path_and_query) in
# proxy.rs; crates/podnet-core/src/hop.rs and exit.rs (the stage and the
# class of a failure, Refused; now on pod_core::Failure) in fail.rs; crates/podnet-core/src/services.rs
# (the facts of the edge) in services.rs.
# tests/: the quick tunnel against the stand-in of the service and of the
# edge (src/standin.rs, feature standin), over the library in place of the
# binary of podnet; the tests of the
# command line (prints_json_lines, stops_clean_on_sigterm_after_ready,
# detach_ps_logs_and_stop) stay in podnet.
